# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
.vs/
/android/
build/
*.tmp
.vscode/
*.depren
flower_sheets/

# GDExtension build output. The addon's own bin/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the
# built library is committed so the addon works from a checkout — but the .dll is the
# only thing there worth keeping; the import library and the linker's leavings are not.
godot-cpp/bin/
godot-cpp/gen/
.sconsign.dblite
src/*.obj
addons/image_wrangler/bin/*.exp
addons/image_wrangler/bin/*.lib
addons/image_wrangler/bin/*.pdb
addons/image_wrangler/bin/~image_wrangler.windows.editor.x86_64.dll

# The vendored Open Image Denoise runtime, committed on purpose — see
# thirdparty/oidn/README-vendored.md. It has to sit beside the extension, because that is
# the only place both Godot's loader and OIDN's own module lookup will find it, which
# puts it squarely under the blanket *.dll above.
#
# Named one file at a time rather than globbed: a re-vendor that drags the CUDA or HIP
# device module back in should be a visible decision, not a silent twenty megabytes.
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/OpenImageDenoise.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/OpenImageDenoise_core.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/OpenImageDenoise_device_cpu.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/tbb12.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/tbbbind.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/tbbbind_2_0.dll
!addons/image_wrangler/bin/tbbbind_2_5.dll

# Raw buffer dumps from the parity harness. Regenerable, and large enough that a
# baseline run of every case would dwarf the repo.
tests/dump/
